    {
      "id": "truthy-string-map",
      "stored": {
        "shp": "yes",
        "gpkg": true,
        "kmz": "no"
      },
      "expected_ts": {
        "schema": "ds.design-output-selection/v1",
        "prints": [],
        "geospatial": [
          "gpkg"
        ],
        "tabular": [],
        "execution": {}
      },
      "expected": {
        "schema": "ds.design-output-selection/v1",
        "prints": [],
        "geospatial": [
          "shp",
          "gpkg"
        ],
        "tabular": []
      },
      "placements": {
        "gpkg": [
          "desktop",
          "web"
        ],
        "shp": [
          "desktop",
          "web"
        ]
      },
      "tokens": [
        "shp",
        "gpkg"
      ],
      "why": "A settings map may record truth as `\"yes\"`/`1`/`on`, and every other reader of this row (`report_formats::string_list`, and therefore `plan` and ds-brain) has always honoured that. The deleted TypeScript accepted only the boolean literal `true`, so it silently dropped `shp` from a selection the report itself produced."
    },
